content.p:
Use the Lurch proof verification system to prove one of these maps P,Q:\mathbb R^3\rightarrow\mathbb R^3 is a linear transformation, and the other is not.
P\left( \left[\begin{array}{c} x \\ y \\ z \end{array}\right] \right)= {{Pmap}}
Q\left( \left[\begin{array}{c} x \\ y \\ z \end{array}\right] \right)= {{Qmap}}
